<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Psalm baseline — created 2026-08-02 alongside the new `composer check:strict`.

  WHY IT EXISTS: `composer psalm` reports 108 errors on this tree (measured in
  nextcloud:32-apache, PHP 8.3.32, psalm 5.26.1). That is not new breakage — the
  shared CI workflow has been running `composer psalm` and FAILING on every run
  for months. Fixing 108 type findings is a real piece of work; it must not be
  the toll gate on making `check:strict` exist at all. The baseline freezes the
  known set so any NEW finding fails the gate.

  WHAT IS IN HERE, and why each family is debt rather than a defect:

  * MixedAssignment x33, MixedArgument x11, MixedMethodCall x2,
    MixedArrayOffset x1 — psalm.xml runs at errorLevel="1" (the strictest
    setting), where every value psalm cannot narrow is an error. These come
    almost entirely from `array<string, mixed>` payload envelopes
    (InstallerService::getAppVersions and friends). Behaviour is correct; the
    annotations are simply looser than errorLevel 1 demands.

  * RedundantConditionGivenDocblockType x16, RedundantCast x6,
    RedundantCastGivenDocblockType x5, RedundantFunctionCall x3,
    RedundantCondition x3, UnnecessaryVarAnnotation x2,
    DocblockTypeContradiction x2, TypeDoesNotContainType x1 — defensive
    `is_string()` / `(string)` guards that psalm can prove unnecessary. Removing
    them is safe only if the docblock is right; they are deliberately kept.

  * DeprecatedMethod x6 — `OCP\IConfig::getAppValue`/`setAppValue`. Real
    upstream deprecations, real migration work (to `IAppConfig`), out of scope
    for a CI-plumbing change. Tracked in the follow-up issue.

  * InvalidReturnStatement x5, InvalidReturnType x1, InvalidArgument x2,
    LessSpecificReturnStatement x1, MoreSpecificReturnType x1,
    NullableReturnStatement x1, InvalidNullableReturnType x1,
    ArgumentTypeCoercion x1 — a genuine shape drift: `InstallerService`'s
    declared return type says each version entry carries `cachedOffline`, but
    `errorEnvelope()` builds entries without it (same drift in
    ForgeReleaseSource::dedupeAndSort for `version`). Unreachable today because
    the error envelopes carry EMPTY lists, so nothing iterates them — but it is
    a real inconsistency and is called out in the follow-up issue rather than
    quietly buried.

  * UndefinedMethod x1 — `Doctrine\DBAL\Schema\Table::getColumn` in
    Version1004Date20260725120000.php. NOT a defect: the method exists in DBAL;
    this app does not require doctrine/dbal, so psalm has no declaration to
    resolve against. A stub gap.

  * PossiblyUndefinedArrayOffset x1, PossiblyNullIterator x1, UnusedVariable x1
    — low-severity local cleanups.

  psalm.xml sets findUnusedBaselineEntry="true", so an entry that stops applying
  becomes an error: the baseline cannot silently rot. Do NOT regenerate this
  file to silence a new finding — fix the finding.
-->
